From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: use pkg-config for ALSA on Linux

CMake cannot infer the compiler ABI under the QEMU user build route, so its
generic FindALSA module omits the openEuler lib64 search path even though the
official alsa-lib-devel package is installed. Resolve the same official ALSA
development files through their pkg-config metadata and link its imported
target.

No bundled ALSA copy is fetched.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of raptor 0.8.1 CMakeLists.txt
Patch-License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -123,11 +123,12 @@ if(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} MATCHES "Android")
         )
 
 elseif(${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} MATCHES "Linux")
-    find_package(ALSA REQUIRED)
+    find_package(PkgConfig REQUIRED)
+    pkg_check_modules(ALSA REQUIRED IMPORTED_TARGET alsa)
     add_executable( ${PROJECT_NAME} ${SOURCE_FILES} )
     target_link_libraries(raptor
         textscreen
-        asound
+        PkgConfig::ALSA
         SDL2::SDL2main
         SDL2::SDL2
         )
-- 
